It is my feeling that even with this trick, nethack is still an SOB.  Although
this is probably a loophole in the wishing scheme, I don't think it will 
detract from the overall game *much*.  Wands of wishing are extremely
difficult to come by (unless there is something I don't know), and so 
I think that it not unreasonable to use tehm in this way.  Which brings
me to another subject.....

/* Enable self-righteous wizard mode */

I find it *HIGHLY* annoying when I get to the 31 level, after fighting
my way through a horde of nasties, and find a wand of wishing with ONE
charge.  Why ONE charge?  Has someone else used it (the wizard perhaps?)
After killing of the inhabitants of the dungeon as far as this level, I
am usually in poor shape to battle those damn minotaurs (who seem more than
able to strip me of 40 or so hit points per attack!).  That wand is usually
the difference between me being able to continue or not.  Maybe I'm not
ready for the lower levels yet, but damn if I know anything in the upper
levels which does prepare you for the lower levels!


/* Disable self-righteous wizard mode */

Okay.....

I'm calm now.  I'm not against the use of this spoiler to gain wishes, 
especially since I consider it a facet of the game to come up with
ingenious solutions to problems.  Maybe the development team feels
differently and will fix this in a later release, but for now, I 
don't see any harm.

